    'about.heading': 'About IsItSafeToTravel',
    'about.project_title': 'About the Project',
    'about.project_text': `IsItSafeToTravel is a free, independently run travel safety platform that provides composite safety scores for 248 countries worldwide. Scores are recomputed every day from ${SOURCE_COUNT_DISPLAY} public sources: travel advisories from ${ADVISORY_GOV_COUNT_DISPLAY} governments plus the World Bank, V-Dem Institute, INFORM Risk Index, Global Peace Index, UCDP, ReliefWeb and GDACS.`,
    'about.mission_title': 'Mission',
    'about.mission_text': 'Our mission is to make travel safety information transparent, accessible, and data-driven. Every score is backed by publicly verifiable sources, and our methodology is fully documented.',
    'about.author_title': 'Author',
    'about.author_text': 'IsItSafeToTravel is created and maintained by Riccardo Dominici, an independent developer and data analyst. The project is built with a focus on data transparency, automated pipelines, and full public documentation of the methodology.',
    'about.sources_title': 'Data Sources',
    'about.sources_text': `We aggregate data from ${SOURCE_COUNT_DISPLAY} public sources updated daily — travel advisories from ${ADVISORY_GOV_COUNT_DISPLAY} governments plus global indices. See our {methodology_link} for full details on how scores are calculated.`,
